Close the departing window only on present or a new generation (review)

Codex review of #34:
- The oracle closed the departing window on any reported documentGeneration,
  so a status still on the departing document (closed/doc-1 after
  navigating/doc-1) armed the old document's late span. The window now
  closes only on present or on a generation different from the stored one,
  and every reported generation (the navigating frame's too) is the latest
  confirmation.
- Three cases pin what the first one left open: a same-document status after
  navigating keeps the window open; an unchanged generation retires nothing;
  a new generation closes the window even when present was missed (pageState
  may be absent from a documentChanged frame).
- test_stale_watchdog asserts the three matching oracle mutants fail.

